# Build context for deploy/Dockerfile is the REPO ROOT (`context: ..` in
# deploy/docker-compose.yml), not deploy/ itself -- so this file has to live here, at the
# root, to have any effect; a .dockerignore under deploy/ would be silently ignored.
#
# Nothing below is COPYed into an image layer today -- deploy/Dockerfile only COPYs
# specific, named paths (pyproject.toml, uv.lock, src/, scripts/, config/, README.md,
# deploy/healthcheck.py), never `COPY . .` -- but every path listed here is still sent to
# the Docker daemon as part of the build context on every `docker compose build`/`up
# --build`, whether or not a COPY instruction ever reads it (fix-round finding, minor #6).
# Secrets specifically (.env*) must never even make that trip: a future edit that adds a
# careless `COPY . .` would otherwise bake them straight into an image layer, and "it
# wasn't in the build context" is a much stronger guarantee than "nothing currently COPYs
# it" when someone edits the Dockerfile six months from now without re-reading this file.

# --- Secrets: never sent to the Docker daemon, under any circumstances ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/recorder.env
!deploy/recorder.env.example

# --- VCS / editors / OS ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store

# --- Python environments / caches ---
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
dist
build
*.egg-info

# --- Data and reports: large, never needed inside the image ---
data
*.parquet
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
research/reports

# --- Claude/agent scratch, docs not needed at runtime ---
.claude
docs
KICKOFF.md
